{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1253161-alchemicals-as-cities-first","id":1253161,"title":"Alchemicals as cities first?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Alchemical Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-10T16:57:10-07:00","id":1253161,"title":"Alchemicals as cities first?","content":"Had an idea after reading through Mummy the Curse, (where you wake when called by your cult with phenominal cosmic power and no memories, and slowly gain memories and loose power), and wondered how that night work as applied to alchemicals. I always liked the idea of them becoming bigger, both physically and spiritually, but they aren\u2019t very \u201cplayable\u201d as a city, and in certain games may never get that far. <br /> <br /> So I was wondering about making them a city first. They are arguably powerful, but mostly just non-sentient caretakers, until something goes wrong and the people cry out for a hero and one is made. Perhaps using the power backwards mechanic from mummy? Slowly loosing juice the longer you stay apart from your city self, you could always plug back in and power up, but that comes at the loss of all the personal connections you made this mortal lifetime, waking again to the mechanical prayers of your lovers great grandchildren. <br /> <br /> Thoughts? Concerns? Is it even implementable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24102-tweedbarista","name":"Tweedbarista","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T17:08:12-07:00","id":1253165,"title":"","content":"Would this be intended as something that operates on a more generational scale, as Mummy does?<br /> <br /> I could see it functioning on a shorter span, but it would seem to me that just results in something very close to the kinds of regular returns to the vats that they already have, in which case, what does the change accomplish?<br /> <br /> I don't think it's an unworkable idea, it just needs to first establish what it wants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T17:57:20-07:00","id":1253176,"title":"","content":"I've considered using the basic outline of the Architect in the corebook as the basis for an Alchemical City's agent with the charms refluffed to be more based on tangible technology in and around the city i.e. being able to profile someone via their home is your city-self pulling up nearby security camera footage and profiling them from that. <br /> <br /> I don't know how that would work in Creation but the main reason I'd do it would be to diversity an Autochthonia game a little.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T20:15:04-07:00","id":1253200,"title":"","content":"The main point of the change would be to try and decouple experience and essence from humanity and memories.<br /> <br /> Those bandits and or gremlins too hard for you to just death laser away? You could always go back to your manse-self and become five essence again, but it may take to long for you to wake back up, and/or you sacrifice the version of you that had loved ones worth protecting, or perhaps to your horror latter, city you decided it was a waste of resources and let your loved ones die. <br /> <br /> Instead of the getting of experience and raising of essence, the natural reward for playing the game, being linked directly to loosing your humanity. It\u2019s always there as a choice, perhaps even one your mortal cult/minders are pressuring you to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24102-tweedbarista","name":"Tweedbarista","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T02:40:29-07:00","id":1253239,"title":"","content":"One fundamental problem I have with this is that the way the Arisen operate isn't particularly efficient, even for the specific function they were designed for. The endless cycle of death and rebirth is pretty much a purpose-built flaw for them, designed by the asshole necromancer-gods to make it hard for them to retain their memory and their humanity at the expense of operational capacity.<br /> <br /> Why would Autochthon, the &quot;god&quot; of invention and industry, who genuinely cares about his human subjects (both because he admires humans for what he believes they share with him and because he needs them to survive the Void), implement such an inefficient scheme when building the protectors of his people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":582,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","user":"Morangias","date":". 09-11-2018, 05:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T03:57:34-07:00","id":1253246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tweedbarista</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1253161-alchemicals-as-cities-first?p=1253200#post1253200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those bandits and or gremlins too hard for you to just death laser away? You could always go back to your manse-self and become five essence again, but it may take to long for you to wake back up, and/or you sacrifice the version of you that had loved ones worth protecting, or perhaps to your horror latter, city you decided it was a waste of resources and let your loved ones die.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would that translate to play? In particular, group play?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tweedbarista</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of the getting of experience and raising of essence, the natural reward for playing the game, being linked directly to loosing your humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>But permanent Clarity is only a detail past Essence 5.<br /> <br /> I would get that if it was a matter of wanting to play the city without Clarity being capped, but the emphasis here seems to be on not playing the city?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T15:37:43-07:00","id":1253727,"title":"","content":"The other idea playing with is the powering down instead of powering up. Fresh out the vat at essence 5 and it just dropping as you, say use certain charms or stray to far from your city (or Laird city willing to lend you power), or maybe act against the wishes of the citizens that awoke them?<br /> <br /> One of the things that I like about the alchemicals is how close and interdependent they are with mortals, both in assembly and operation of municipal charms and so on. I\u2019d like to see a city with a slightly corrupt board that calls on their hero to do less savory things, and he is faced with the delema. Or a devoted cult that works for their pop idol queens hapiness, to the point of diverting resources to keep her moving long enough to find love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24102-tweedbarista","name":"Tweedbarista","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T03:40:53-07:00","id":1253836,"title":"","content":"Another issue: the amount of Charms the Alchemical can install is dependent on their Personal Mote Pool, which will diminish as they drop in Essence. What happens to Charms in excess of the Alchemical's new limit? Do they just drop off their body? Which ones? What if all their Charms are clustered in a couple big Arrays? These Charms are priceless artifacts, so I presume the Alchemical will have to pick the dropped ones up and carry them back to the vault complex... have fun doing it four times per activation.<br /> <br /> Seriously, I like Mummy the Curse a lot, but I also like Alchemicals a lot, and these are two great tastes that don't go well together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T08:42:04-07:00","id":1253898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1253161-alchemicals-as-cities-first?p=1253836#post1253836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another issue: the amount of Charms the Alchemical can install is <b>dependent on their Personal Mote Pool</b>, which will diminish as they drop in Essence. What happens to Charms in excess of the Alchemical's new limit? Do they just drop off their body? Which ones? What if all their Charms are clustered in a <b>couple big Arrays</b>? These Charms are priceless artifacts, so I presume the Alchemical will have to pick the dropped ones up and carry them back to the vault complex... have fun doing it four times per activation.<br /> <br /> Seriously, I like Mummy the Curse a lot, but I also like Alchemicals a lot, and these are two great tastes that don't go well together.</div> </div> </div> </div>bolding mine. <br /> <br /> These are concepts built in to the 2E's Alchemcial's paradigm. I don't think it's wise to assume that they'll stick around in 3E. There's a completely new dynamic in play after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T09:07:48-07:00","id":1253905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1253161-alchemicals-as-cities-first?p=1253898#post1253898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">bolding mine.<br /> <br /> These are concepts built in to the 2E's Alchemcial's paradigm. I don't think it's wise to assume that they'll stick around in 3E. There's a completely new dynamic in play after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I don't think we have any grounds for discussion if we dismiss the 2e considerations of a splat that doesn't yet exist in 3e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T09:43:04-07:00","id":1253928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1253161-alchemicals-as-cities-first?p=1253905#post1253905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I don't think we have any grounds for discussion if we dismiss the 2e considerations of a splat that doesn't yet exist in 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can with most things due to 1e but alchemicals was impoved by 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T10:37:37-07:00","id":1253960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1253161-alchemicals-as-cities-first?p=1253905#post1253905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I don't think we have any grounds for discussion if we dismiss the 2e considerations of a splat that doesn't yet exist in 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait you're saying that if your argument is shaky, the entire idea presented by the thread is shaky?<br /> <br /> The mechanics of 2e have never had strong influence on discussions involving 3e stuff. The most important thing is that whatever you add to 3e <i>works in 3e</i>. So stating that an idea is bad in 3e because of the mechanical implementation of things in 2e is an inherently flawed argument.<br /> <br /> If you don't like Alchemicals starting as cities then just say that. Don't try to justify your dislike with 2e mechanics, and <i>definitely</i> don't think you're gonna make a discussion of hypotheticals go away just because someone calls you out on how shaky your argument is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T14:55:02-07:00","id":1254012,"title":"","content":"I could see it in a 2.5 game, some kind of special top-secret municipal charm: It's already in the fluff that the exact location of a alchy-city's soulgem is a state secret (because its a single point of failure) - so a special municipal charm that can release the alchy's soulgem and implant it in an essence 5 avatar<br /> <br /> maybe have it as a fancy submodule to the Avatar-launching silo charm? Instead of implanting soul-echo imprints, implant the soulgem of the city as a means of escape?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T17:25:14-07:00","id":1254034,"title":"","content":"I don't think I care for this.<br /> <br /> For starters, it seems alien to ideas that I consider core to their being. Alchemicals, after all, are reincarnated heroes whose exaltation is rooted in their human achievements through multiple lifetimes. Making them start as a city makes any human-like qualities to their character more like an accident, developing on a recently-built engine of civic purpose.<br /> <br /> This also dooms them in ways that would make Abyssals wince: From the moment they emerge from their city, the clock is ticking. Perhaps it can be temporarily stopped, perhaps it can even be pushed back depending on implementation, but these Alchemicals are set in a position where the entropy that works to claim them erodes their own passion and agency. That's not to say that Clarity didn't serve a bit of this function re: passions, but it's still different since an as-written Alchemical still serves the same general goals. The agency, however, is a harder pill to swallow: if you as a player are at all invested in your character's intimacies, it means that an Alchemical who gives in to the need to rest and recharge is potentially committing suicide. Your city-self, on the other hand seems like it would be almost inimical to you as an individual, rather than genuinely benevolent.<br /> <br /> This is an interesting concept--very interesting, narratively--but I really don't know if I'd go for it as a player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T20:04:04-07:00","id":1254073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1253161-alchemicals-as-cities-first?p=1253836#post1253836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another issue: the amount of Charms the Alchemical can install is dependent on their Personal Mote Pool, which will diminish as they drop in Essence. What happens to Charms in excess of the Alchemical's new limit? Do they just drop off their body? Which ones? What if all their Charms are clustered in a couple big Arrays? These Charms are priceless artifacts, so I presume the Alchemical will have to pick the dropped ones up and carry them back to the vault complex... have fun doing it four times per activation.<br /> <br /> Seriously, I like Mummy the Curse a lot, but I also like Alchemicals a lot, and these are two great tastes that don't go well together.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of mummy but it unfortunately really only has one kind of game in group play. I don't think it really works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T02:43:10-07:00","id":1254122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1253161-alchemicals-as-cities-first?p=1253960#post1253960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait you're saying that if your argument is shaky, the entire idea presented by the thread is shaky?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's not at all what I'm saying. However, if I did say that, I'd be right within the paradigm you presented - if my argument is shaky because it's based on 2e mechanics, then so is the OP's idea, which is based on such 2e mechanics as Alchemicals increasing in size past Essence 5, City-size Alchemicals being permanently saddled with Clarity, and Colossus- and City-sized Alchemicals being able to spawn a human-sized drone body. We don't know if any of those will be true in 3e either, do we? Hence, shaky idea based on 2e mechanics.<br /> <br /> Thus, ironically, you are defeated by your own strawman.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mechanics of 2e have never had strong influence on discussions involving 3e stuff. The most important thing is that whatever you add to 3e <i>works in 3e</i>. So stating that an idea is bad in 3e because of the mechanical implementation of things in 2e is an inherently flawed argument. </div> </div> </div>The thing is, while 3e isn't shy to change things around from previous editions when necessary, it doesn't change things just for shits and giggles. Splats we've currently seen in 3e may differ in the minutiae of mechanical implementation, but they are fundamentally recognizable as the same entities - Solars are still top dogs whose powers go from peak human capability to superhuman, shining perfection, Dragon-Blooded are still individually weakest Exalted with flashy elemental powers, and Lunars are still Attribute-based shapeshifters.<br /> <br /> In this vein, Alchemicals have always been limited in how many Charms they can install at once, and this limitation has always been expressed through Charms having installation costs that can only be paid from their Personal Pool. This was true in both 1e and 2e (except in the case of Alchemicals, 1e doesn't really matter, as it's probably the only splat on which everyone agrees 2e version was straight up better). Arrays have likewise existed in both previous editions, and have even survived the culling of their conceptual progenitor, the Combo mechanic, in 2.5, because of how they factored into the aforementioned limitation. Given how important it is for Alchemical play experience, installation costs are extremely unlikely to disappear in 3e, especially since nothing about them clashes with any mechanical aspect of 3e that differentiates it from 2e. Admittedly, Arrays might just go away, as they really lost a lot of their value when Combos stopped being a thing, but their existence has barely any effect on the crux of my argument.<br /> <br /> In other words, I'm not pointing out issues with how the proposed change affects edition-specific mechanics (which would indeed be a flawed argument, I'll give you that). I'm pointing out issues with how the proposed change affects a core splat theme. And that's a perfectly valid argument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you don't like Alchemicals starting as cities then just say that. Don't try to justify your dislike with 2e mechanics, and <i>definitely</i> don't think you're gonna make a discussion of hypotheticals go away just because someone calls you out on how shaky your argument is. </div> </div> </div>The problem with discussing hypotheticals is that in vacuum, all ideas are equally valid. If we assume every potential issue with the OPs idea is simply not an issue without specifying why, then sure, the OPs idea works! Except, what are we discussing here? The most you can say about it under such assumptions is &quot;I like it&quot; or &quot;I don't like it&quot;. To discuss anything more, we need some benchmark for the idea, some frame of reference. And since we're discussing a possible depiction of Alchemical Exalted, the most logical frame of reference we have are the Alchemical Exalted we already have, i.e. their 1e and 2e depictions (except, again, mostly 2e because it's better in pretty much every way). Hence, I have contributed to the thread by pointing out a major splat theme that's going to clash with the proposed changes. Now this is something the OP can think about and refine their idea.<br /> <br /> This is independent of my overall dislike of the idea, which BTW I have &quot;just said that&quot;, right under pointing out the specific issue, in a separate paragraph so it's clearly marked as a separate thought. So I'm really not sure what you expected of me. But the next time you feel the need to lecture me, please make sure you have a case first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T05:11:17-07:00","id":1254139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1253161-alchemicals-as-cities-first?p=1254073#post1254073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of mummy but it unfortunately really only has one kind of game in group play. I don't think it really works.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first time I've read MtC, it seemed really prohibitive. Upon second reading, I've paid more attention to the mechanics involved rather than how it's described in narrative terms, and while you're still very much on a leash, it's a pretty long one, as a single Descent can easily last you a couple months or more before you get to shenanigans that could possibly prolong it even further. There's still the matter of &quot;why would multiple undead demigods be awakened at the same time with compatible goals&quot;, but the adventure included in the corebook doesn't seem to make such a big deal out of it. MtC might be the only game I know where the stoytelling chapter actually tries to make things more complicated for you than they ought to be.<br /> <br /> This is all regarding MtC as its own game. As a potential inspiration for Alchemicals, I feel the themes (and mechanics meant to evoke said themes) are clashing beyond any hopes of reconciliation. Alchies are all about close cooperation between themselves and mortals, Mummies are about tense, distrustful cooperation between themselves and a complicated, highly formalized relations with mortals. Alchies work best when they come prepared for the particular problem, Mummies are all about powering through all obstacles on the go, because every delay costs you precious mojo. Alchies struggle to maintain hold on their humanity, Mummies have to regain it from zero. To change Alchemicals to more resemble how Mummies work would strip them of many things that make them Alchemicals in the first place.<br /> <br /> That's not to say I'd have a problem with a type of Exalted operating more like the Arisen. It's just I'd rather make them a separate type of Exalted rather than try to fit a cog-shaped peg into a sarcophagus-shaped hole <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T05:22:35-07:00","id":1254141,"title":"","content":"The idea of disappearing into tombs for extended stints and intermittently popping out to go about some grim business is an image I've had for what might become of some Abyssal Exalted in the long term. A kind of refined form of the Chivalry of Death that keeps them on message without a sense that the amount of time that they're taking renders them ineffectual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}